course: dictionary
lesson: 12384
title: Words for the big finish
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how something ends. Culminate is one of them. It means to reach the highest or final point of something, often after a long time or many steps. «The school year culminated in a big concert.» The year had many weeks of lessons, and the concert was the final high point at the end.
explain: Culminate is a formal word, so you will meet it in history books, sports reports and stories. Look for the clue words around it. It is usually followed by «in» or «with», as in «culminated in» or «culminated with». Those little words tell you what the final point was.
explain: Remember the context check: swap in a simpler word and see if the sentence still makes sense. «Our long climb culminated in a view from the top» works the same as «Our long climb ended in a view from the top». Ended is a simpler word, but culminated also tells the reader that the ending was the highest point of the climb.
fact: Culminate means to reach the highest or final point of something.
fact: It often means the end of a long time or many steps.
fact: Culminate is usually followed by «in» or «with».
fact: «Culminated» is the past form, as in «The match culminated with a goal».
fact: Culminate, culminates, culminated and culminating are all forms of the same verb.
exercise: «The school year culminated in a big concert.» What does culminated mean here? | Was cancelled | *Reached its final high point | Started again from the beginning | Got quieter and quieter
exercise: «Our long climb culminated in a view from the top.» Which word could replace culminated without changing the meaning? | slept through | *ended up at | ran away from | forgot about
exercise: Copy the word that tells you what the ending was: «The match culminated with a goal.» | with | culminated | match | *goal
test: «Months of practice culminated in a prize for Maya.» What does culminated mean? | Was forgotten | Fell apart slowly | Started a new month | *Came to a final high point
test: Fill the gap: Yesterday the show ___ in a big finale. | culminates | *culminated | culminating | culminate
exam: Fill the gap: Every summer the sports camp ___ with a big race. | culminated | culminate | culminating | *culminates
